The theme resolver in this directory (theme.go) is an independent Go
implementation whose structure and semantics follow Monaco Editor's token
theme (src/vs/editor/common/languages/supports/tokenization.ts: TokenTheme,
parseTokenTheme, resolveParsedTokenThemeRules, ThemeTrieElement) and its
standalone theme handling of editor.foreground/editor.background and base
theme inheritance (src/vs/editor/standalone/browser/standaloneThemeService.ts;
monaco-editor 0.56.0). The base theme data it loads is embedded by
ui/editor/langs (see ui/editor/langs/NOTICE).

The table of default editor colors in ui/editor/paint.go (monacoDefaults:
editor.background, editor.foreground, editor.selectionBackground,
editor.inactiveSelectionBackground, editorLineNumber.foreground,
editorLineNumber.activeForeground, editor.lineHighlightBorder,
editorCursor.foreground, editorGutter.background, for the vs, vs-dark,
hc-black and hc-light bases) copies the values Monaco registers as color
defaults (monaco-editor 0.56.0:
esm/vs/platform/theme/common/colors/editorColors.js,
esm/vs/editor/common/core/editorColorRegistry.js,
esm/vs/platform/theme/common/colors/baseColors.js), covered by the same
notice below.

